# CODEOWNERS — paths that always require Jon's review before merge.
#
# To actually ENFORCE this file, the repo's branch protection ruleset for
# `main` and `v3/main` must have "Require review from Code Owners" enabled.
# Without that setting the file is advisory only. Documented here either way
# so the policy intent is in the repo.
#
# Pattern rules:
#   * Last matching pattern wins per file (so put broader rules first)
#   * `*` is the catch-all default owner
#
# This file pairs with .github/workflows/auto-merge.yml:
#   - auto-merge fires on PRs labeled rollback-safe + adversarial-reviewed
#     + NOT needs-jon-approval
#   - A PR touching a CODEOWNERS path adds Jon as a required reviewer; once
#     he approves, the auto-merge workflow can still complete the merge.
#   - For paths that must NEVER auto-merge regardless, the convention is to
#     ALSO add the `needs-jon-approval` label at PR open time.

# Catch-all — everything has Jon as the default owner.
*                                           @JDC000000

